# Indic Transformer MT

English to Hindi translation with a Transformer implemented from scratch in PyTorch, following "Attention Is All You Need" (Vaswani et al., 2017).

## Implemented
- Scaled dot-product and multi-head attention, padding and causal masks
- Sinusoidal positional encoding, encoder and decoder stacks, shared embeddings
- Adam with the paper's warmup schedule, label smoothing, token-budget batching
- Greedy and beam search decoding; SacreBLEU and chrF++ evaluation on FLORES-200
- 23 unit tests (`uv run pytest -v`)

## Pilot baseline (18.7K sentence pairs, small model)
| Metric | Result |
|---|---|
| Best validation loss | about 4.56 (perplexity about 96) |
| BLEU / chrF++ (greedy, first 100 FLORES dev sentences) | 0.46 / 10.36 |

A near-zero BLEU is expected at this data size. The project studies how quality changes with more data.

## Status
In progress: data-efficiency experiment, pretrained baseline, error analysis.

Data: IITB English-Hindi (non-commercial research use) and FLORES-200. Datasets are downloaded by the scripts and are not stored in this repo.